Optional — Deferred capabilities
These items are recorded for later consideration and are excluded from current WF1–Admin implementation and release acceptance. They require an explicit scoped decision, versioned contracts and tests before activation. Existing authorization, privacy, mandatory byte validation and Admin approval remain required.
1. Screen-reader support and verification
Defer the dedicated TalkBack/VoiceOver interaction and screen-reader acceptance campaign. Future work defines meaningful labels, focus order, dynamic announcements and representative-device tests. This deferral does not count as completed accessibility certification and does not require removal of existing semantic controls.
2. Static WebP intake
Current intake remains JPEG/PNG and MP4/H.264. Static WebP support is deferred: before enabling, define MIME/magic-byte and decode validation, dimensions/size, animation rejection, original/hash/provenance handling, Python pre/full analysis, derivatives and fixtures. Do not accept WebP solely by filename or silently expand the whitelist.
3. Additional consistency scoring
CV, GPS and media-quality inputs use the current availability-aware WF1 calculation. PhoBERT NLP is part of the active WF1 contract. Only the additional consistency component stays deferred; it requires an independent mapping/calibration that does not duplicate CV or NLP evidence. Do not double-count CV as a synthetic NLP/consistency signal or claim unavailable models executed.
4. WF1/WF2 shared evidence reader
Combining assessed published claims with eligible votes in WF1 confidence is deferred. A future version must specify source/version/context alignment, one observation per contributor across sources, current author exclusions, accuracy/history/recency snapshot, migration/replay and coexistence tests. Current WF2 votes are aggregated independently for review; they never automatically publish or mutate facts.
5. Additional scoring extensions
Temporal-corroboration bonuses and learned weights require a separate versioned calibration proposal with abuse and regression tests. They are absent from v3-metrics-3. Retired single-score trust multipliers, automatic publication, score-based rejection/supplement requests and legacy +50/−100 rules are discarded policies, not optional implementation paths.

